abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For normalized Rademacher sums with coefficients capped by a, a sharp inverse theorem for large support gaps, sharp stability of the support-gap optimum at every cap with optimal constant sqrt(2+sqrt(2)), and the exact nonlinear saturated modulus, all formalized in Lean; and the exact Kolmogorov-distance cap optimum for 1/sqrt(5) <= a <= 1/sqrt(3), conditional on the completed Keller-Klein comparison and using the Hollom-Portier tail profile, Tomaszewski's theorem and validated interval certificates. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
